WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
<b>Noboribetsu</b>

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:06.190
So he was pretending to be a masseur 
while spying on our movements?

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.540
The owner of this skin was a very brave man.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.610
Ariko noticed something about the tattoos.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.180
It reminded me of the tattoos 
on my grandmother's arms.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.700
Perhaps that has something to 
do with the code, I thought.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.620
Oh?

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:31.010
Are these all the skins you have, Lieutenant?

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.010
Indeed.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:38.220
But, Ariko, I'm amazed you found the 
skin in the middle of that avalanche.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.420
I was lucky, that's all.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.390
The man's legs were sticking out of the snow.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.470
If we weren't lucky, the skin might've 
ended up fertilizing the mountain flowers,

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.370
or feeding wild dogs.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.520
And given that even a single missing skin

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.820
will stop us from finding 
the gold together...

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.910
A terrifying thought, isn't it?

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.880
Well, Ariko?

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.540
Does it seem similar at 
all to the Ainu tattoos?

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.000
<b>I
B
U
R
I</b>

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:12.000
<b>H
I
D
A
K
A</b>

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:12.000
<b>T
O
K
A
C
H
I</b>

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:12.000
<b>K
I
T
A
M
I</b>

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.640
Ainu tattoos differ by region.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.380
I thought perhaps that was a clue 
to where the gold was hidden.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.000
But right now, I can't say.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.470
I see.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.930
But that's interesting to hear.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.350
Ariko, the moon's the same, isn't it?

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.850
What's this about the moon?

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.980
You and I spent a night 
calling out to each other

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.240
in a trench at the Battle of Mukden.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.860
The only thing we could see in the 
darkness was the thin sliver of moon.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.320
The moon's the one thing that 
hasn't changed since then.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>T
H
E
 
N
E
X
T
 
N
I
G
H
T</b>

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.930
Umph!

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.000
Watch your step, Admiral Koito.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.510
It's a new moon tonight.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.520
Where are they?

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:13.990
Come on!

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.190
Did you get them?

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.990
I got them all!

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:07.660
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:55.310
<b>Episode Forty-Two
Sweet Lies</b>

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.370
I see footprints here!

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.540
Don't let him get away!

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:00.550
There's a sheer rock wall to our right,
 and round rocks to our left.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:05.230
If we keep going, we'll meet 
a dead end between the cliffs.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.050
Let's turn back.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.180
Watch out for fallen trees.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:14.190
The smell of blood is terrible. 
Can you make it over the mountain?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.510
Yes.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.650
<b>S
E
V
E
R
A
L
 
H
O
U
R
S
 
E
A
R
L
I
E
R</b>

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:33.050
What's this makiri doing here?

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:38.130
It was Lieutenant Tsurumi who took what was 
left from the murder scene in Tomakomai.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:45.340
He knows that your father was one of 
the seven Ainu killed by Nopperabo.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.190
I'm disappointed.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:51.690
You forgot the moon we saw 
from the trenches, didn't you?

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:58.130
The tattooed skin you brought 
me didn't belong to Toni Anji.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:06.490
I guess Hijikata Toshizou was unaware 
that we already knew what his skin said.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:12.750
He put you up to this, I assume. Told you 
to follow in your father's footsteps?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.260
There's no going back now.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.010
You chose the worst of all possible paths.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.910
<i>He's still alive.</i>

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.110
Ariko Ipopte...

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:49.410
I'll tell you the one big difference 
between me and Hijikata Toshizou.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:55.640
His plan for Hokkaido's independence 
requires the support and trust of the Ainu.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:00.920
That's why he could never exact 
real revenge for your betrayal.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.950
But I'm different.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:09.000
I can punish anyone, Japanese or Ainu.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.890
Like Ikaripopo, the mother of Ariko Ipopte.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.800
And his older brother, Yayuhuyka.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.260
And his older sister, Rerasuye, 
who married a man in Hidaka.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.100
And his nephews Isoninpa and Tumasinu.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.720
Private Ariko!

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.120
You are to take all these 
to Hijikata Toshizou,

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.200
and earn their trust.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.110
You'll be my double agent.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.390
You can do that, right?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.350
Good. With that settled,

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:40.210
I'd like to make it look like you 
had to really work to earn them.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.420
Usami, do it.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:46.510
With pleasure.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.340
Ariko, grit your teeth.

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:59.090
Run fast, Ariko.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.790
I won't tell the men I send after you a thing.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.430
One, two...

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:10.150
Wait, let me rest!
I'm an old man who can't see!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.000
We're not far enough away yet.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.120
If we don't go another day 
without rest, we'll be caught.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.150
There.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:24.710
You're a mess.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.270
I'm so tired...

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.090
I was found when I tried to steal the skins.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.510
Did you get them?

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:36.890
Sekiya's skin, which Ariko 
pretended was Toni Anji's,

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.890
as well as the five possessed
 by Lieutenant Tsurumi.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.710
Six in all.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.650
Is this all?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.320
It's all he showed me.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.250
Is it possible that there were others?

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.490
I'm told that one is worn 
by its bearer at all times.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.620
I stole it at bath time. 
It should be in here.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:02.840
I know he needed to earn the enemy's trust,

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.150
but was it okay to turn 
over every skin we have?

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:07.500
Wouldn't a paper copy have worked, as well?

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.670
It's important that they be on skin.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.590
Paper can be easily faked.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:19.350
The one that Ariko brought wasn't 
Toni Anji's skin, but it was real.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:26.040
This is a copy, and the only reason 
I can trust it is that I made it myself.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:31.860
To anyone but me, it's much less trustworthy.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.790
The fact that it's on skin proves its real.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:39.620
That's why Edogai-kun's tattooed 
skins are so valuable.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.580
Edogai-kun?

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:47.210
The five given to Ariko are all clever 
fakes made from real human skin.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.710
Fakes? Is that possible?

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:55.060
It's entirely possible that Hijikata 
Toshizou will crack the code before we do.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:09:00.220
If that happens, the fakes 
will prove to be of immense value.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.100
What do you think about that Ainu guy?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.100
We need to be careful with him.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.170
It was a cruel thing to do to Ariko,

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:15.530
but I sent him with that skin knowing they'd 
realize it didn't belong to Toni Anji.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:20.350
I saw with my own eyes that 
Sugimoto Saichi was taken in

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:24.040
by Lieutenant Tsurumi after
 being shot at Abashiri.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:28.250
Which means that the copy of Toni 
Anji's skin would've been confiscated.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:35.680
The fact that he made it here alive means 
one of two things: either he's a spy,

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:40.510
or Lieutenant Tsurumi deliberately 
allowed the skins to be stolen.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:45.660
Either way, these skins are likely fake.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:48.520
But that's what I wanted.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:53.030
Add these five to the one 
we found at the taxidermist,

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.280
and it matches that "human taxidermy."

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.800
What's important is that the tattooed 
skins are made from real human skin.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:05.210
If any other skin tattoos were mixed in, 
it would cause a great deal of trouble.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.470
We're extremely fortunate to have all of them

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:09.800
in our possession before they were spread.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:13.870
These skins are half-truths that are 
incredibly close to being a full truths.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:20.640
The plot to use Ariko against us 
ended up going massively in our favor.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:26.440
We'll need to keep Asirpa carefully protected.
 She's the key to cracking the code.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.740
We head to Karafuto!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:34.070
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.460
Toh! Toh! To!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.630
Toh! Toh! To!

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.840
Toh! Toh! To!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:45.990
<i>Ryu was promoted to isohseta, 
the lead dog pulling Sugimoto's sled.</i>

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:49.920
Toh! Toh! To!

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:49.920
Ryu looks so good with 
that thing on his head!

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.920
<b>Enonoka's
Village</b>

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.420
<b>Henke's
Lead
Dog</b>

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.190
Dogs capable of becoming 
the lead dog on a sled team

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.590
are treated better than the other dogs.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.640
They're allowed to sleep 
inside with their owners.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:09.300
Ryu would be treated 
better if he stayed here.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.650
He's found a place where he belongs.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.540
Thanks for everything, Ryu.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:14.650
Thanks.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:17.900
A passing horse sled is going to Oodomari.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.900
I asked them to give us a ride.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.910
We'll say our goodbyes to 
Henke and Enonoka here.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:27.800
She really is a grown-up little girl.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.220
Enonoka...

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.760
We'll wait for you.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.050
Go talk to her.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.010
I won't say goodbye. I'll wait for you.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.250
Don't lose your hohchiri when you cut it off.

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:55.310
Don't forget me.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.780
I won't forget.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.780
Get on! We're leaving!

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.780
I'll come back, Enonoka!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.280
Bye, old man!

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.850
Stay healthy, all of you!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.840
Cikapasi!

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:30.810
Enonoka, wait for me! I'll—

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:33.320
Stop the sled.

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:34.270
One of us fell off.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.800
You okay, Cikapasi?

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.630
Hurry up!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.400
We'll leave you behind!

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.290
What's gotten into him?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.290
Give me a second.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.180
Tanigaki Nispa.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:17.560
Cikapasi... You stay here,

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:21.150
and make yourself a real family.

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:22.970
Yeah.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:27.910
Inkarmat's like me, all alone.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:31.030
You be her family, Tanigaki Nispa.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.030
I'll give you this gun.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:43.670
I inherited it from the 
man who saved my life.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:48.340
Use it to hunt, and repay Henke and 
the others for what they did for us.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:52.060
But don't use it until you're grown up.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.000
I won't be with you to hold you.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.940
When you use it, stand up by yourself.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.740
Stand up by myself...

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.440
I'll be like a boner, won't I, Tanigaki Nispa?

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:07.950
Yes! You will be a boner, Cikapasi.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:12.410
Make sure you bring Asirpa 
home and cheer up Huci!

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:14.780
Yes, I will.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.330
Bye, Cikapasi!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.670
Live a good life!

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:34.180
<b>Oodomari</b>

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.060
Lieutenant Tsurumi is arriving
 tomorrow, it seems.

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.190
You don't look happy.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:48.190
There's something I have to ask 
you before Lieutenant Tsurumi arrives.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.070
Very well.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:54.330
What Ogata said to me at Ako,
 just before he fled...

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:56.700
Barchonok.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.750
He also said this...

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:09.190
Next time you see Lieutenant Tsurumi, 
ask him about the Manchurian Railroad.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:14.030
The South Manchuria Railway Company.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:17.570
We won railway rights to Manchuria as 
a result of the Russo-Japanese War.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.790
This "railway company," however,

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.270
would serve as a de facto 
expansion of Japanese territory.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:28.740
One member of the army, however, violently 
resisted the plan and said it would fail.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.740
That was General Hanazawa Koujirou, 
the former commander of the 7th Division.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:38.240
Only after his suicide did the plans for 
the South Manchuria Railway Company advance.

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.870
After returning from the Russo-Japanese War,
 didn't Lieutenant Tsurumi say...

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:46.520
that our comrades still lie beneath 
the cold Manchurian wastes?

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:52.920
That if Manchuria were Japanese territory, 
their bones would rest in Japan.

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:58.260
Does this mean Lieutenant Tsurumi was 
involved in General Hanazawa's death?

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:03.290
If we assume that Ogata Hyakunosuke joined 
Lieutenant Tsurumi's plan for a revolution

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.840
because he was angry at 
the central government

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.490
for forcing his father to commit suicide,

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:11.030
only to find out the truth at some point 
and betray him, everything makes sense.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.780
But then why tell me?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:19.630
He'd say anything to cause 
confusion in our ranks.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:23.290
Why, at this point, would you 
believe a word Ogata says?

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.920
Barchonok.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:30.550
Ogata was among the masked men 
that kidnapped me in Hakodate.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.300
<b>Travel Inn</b>

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:35.300
I've never met Lieutenant Tsurumi.

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:37.720
What's he like?

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.150
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.890
What will happen if they find the gold?

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:46.810
If nothing else, nobody will 
come after you anymore.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.230
No. What happens to the Ainu?

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.390
If they want Hokkaido to 
be an independent state,

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:54.360
they won't want to make enemies of them.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.870
They'll need laborers, if nothing else.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.190
We can negotiate to ensure that 
any demands you have are met.

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:02.870
You're the only one that can crack the code,

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.890
which means we completely 
have the upper hand.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.380
Ogata?

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:16.720
The masked men were Russians. 
You saw their corpses.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:20.680
Were you one of the masked 
men too, Tsukishima?

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.240
Calm down, Lieutenant Koito.

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:26.010
The whole thing was a sham, 
a show put on for me and my father!

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.870
You wanted to pretend to rescue us,

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:31.320
so you could get access to the Oominato 
Torpedo Group my father commands!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:37.560
Ogata mentioned the Manchurian Railway 
to me because he wanted me to know

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:42.790
that the two of us were just Lieutenant 
Tsurumi's pawns, just like General Hanazawa!

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.730
Am I wrong, Tsukishima?

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.580
These are ridiculous, paranoid fantasies.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:47.740
Enough!

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:49.170
I'll ask him myself!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:52.670
I'll find out the truth 
in front of my father.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:56.470
You <i>were</i> saved, weren't you?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.470
What?

00:17:58.870 --> 00:17:59.890
I had no idea that Ogata

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.970
knew of the connection between the 
Manchurian Railway and General Hanazawa.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:08.190
I was sure his plan was to turn Lieutenant
 Tsurumi over to the central authorities.

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.940
What was he upset about?

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:13.860
He should've been satisfied 
that he got to kill his father.

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:16.890
Ogata killed his father?

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:21.410
Tsurumi put on another little play 
for me. A very complex one.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.880
The soldier really was from Sado, I assume.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:28.870
But after the war, I realized...

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:32.140
There was no reason for somebody 
from Niigata's 2nd Division

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:34.380
to be in that field hospital.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:41.390
<b>Mukden</b>

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:41.390
<b>7th Division</b>

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:41.390
<b>2nd Division</b>

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.560
On that day,

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:41.390
the 2nd Division was a full sixty 
kilometers away, fighting in the mountains.

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:44.500
Tsurumi revealed the trick after nine years,

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:49.890
tearing open old wounds and pouring 
his own love in to fill the hole.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:54.580
That should tell you how 
hard he worked to save me.

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:56.740
To create an army that 
would lay down their lives for him,

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:00.210
that would do anything, no matter how dirty.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:03.520
But, well, it doesn't bother me.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:08.790
My life was never worth enough that I could
 get mad at someone for using me.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:13.430
He wants to use the Ainu gold 
to finance an arms industry

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:15.550
that makes full use of 
Hokkaido's vast resources,

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:18.320
then start a revolution to establish 
his own military government,

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.800
thus improving the status of the 7th Division.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:25.200
And after that, ensure that Manchuria, 
where our comrades sleep,

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.750
is de facto Japanese territory.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.390
What's wrong with any of that?

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:34.980
Is that Lieutenant Tsurumi's final goal?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.760
I don't know his true goal.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:41.490
He excels at using sweet lies to save people.

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:50.070
But if where he's going requires a 
revolution or an invasion of Manchuria...

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:53.350
Then the people who follow him will be saved.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.380
And I see nothing wrong with that.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:59.510
Tsukishima, why do you...

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:05.470
Only people like that can 
ever do big things, right?

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:09.230
I want to watch Lieutenant Tsurumi's 
drama from a front-row seat...

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:10.480
Until the curtain falls.

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:14.920
It would be smart to keep 
this all to yourself.

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:19.100
Lieutenant Tsurumi would think nothing 
of killing you, if he had to.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:24.360
And I would be the one to do his dirty work.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:36.290
Lieutenant Tsurumi is <i>awesome</i>!

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:41.130
Does that mean that even our chance 
meeting in Kagoshima was staged?

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.700
He even staged a fake kidnapping?!

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:46.220
I'm so happy he needs me so badly!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.740
I can't wait to see him! 
I can't wait to see Lieutenant Tsurumi!

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.210
I can't wait! I can't wait!

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:54.730
I can't wait to see Lieutenant Tsurumi!

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:04.330
Huh? Couldn't sleep, Immortal Sugimoto-san?

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:07.300
You're gonna hand over 
Asirpa-chan to the soldiers

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:10.030
and be Lieutenant Tsurumi's little doggie, right?

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.810
It's not like that!

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:17.330
If you were gonna join the guy, 
you should've done it at Otaru!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:21.450
He used to be a lone wolf type. 
Wouldn't hook up with anybody!

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:23.130
Huh, so he softened up.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:25.830
Things are different now!

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:30.480
Once they crack the code, Lieutenant Tsurumi
 and his men won't need Asirpa-san!

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:34.810
They won't force her to fight for 
the Ainu, like Hijikata Toshizou would!

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.620
When you think about what's best 
for her, it's the only choice!

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:40.860
Asirpa-san! Asirpa-san!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:45.110
What happened to giving money to 
that widow you were in love with?

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:47.530
I made a deal to get the money.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:50.130
For enough money for her to get treatment.

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:53.070
And how much do I get?

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:58.330
I didn't put up with all this 
shit for a few hundred yen!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:01.000
You're always obsessed with money!

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:08.800
So you're gonna be the one to guide 
Asirpa-chan to the right path?

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.600
She ain't your lover, 
your wife, or your daughter!

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:15.980
I don't like people who try 
to tie me down, either.

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:18.310
Shut up and go home!

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:22.160
You're just a shriveled up, tired husk of 
a man who can't go on adventures anymore,

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:27.280
so he's trying to convince himself 
he's got something to protect!

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:31.660
You didn't see Asirpa-chan in Karafuto!

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:35.390
She learned a whole lot and grew up!

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:38.750
She's not the girl she was when you met her!

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:43.930
You finally met each other again 
in Karafuto, but you're still apart.

00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:47.670
What Kiroranke taught her wasn't a lie!

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:54.180
He dragged her all the way to Karafuto 
so she could see what it's like up there!

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:59.130
If Asirpa-chan says she 
wants to lead the Ainu,

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:01.300
knowing exactly what that means,
 then let her do it!

00:23:01.300 --> 00:23:04.330
If you just believed in her 
as your partner and an equal,

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:07.530
then you could go back to the 
dangerous man you used to be!

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.090
And you don't honestly believe Lieutenant
 Tsurumi cares about the Ainu, do you?

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:15.540
What do you mean?

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:22.460
I farted.

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:33.240
Prepare to make land!

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Fleeing Karafuto</b>

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:39.170
Next time: "Fleeing Karafuto"!
